ding property taxes totaling approximately Rs 10 crore. These defaulters must attend a hearing on October 5 to sidestep property confiscation. The municipality is also pursuing tax recovery from governmental offices and will publish an updated defaulter roster post the August 31 payment deadline.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/panchkula-civic-body-issues-final-warning-to-100-property-tax-defaulters/134560609?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-61652/134560609.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}